# Reproduction of the multi-subproject reloadOutput duplication bug.
# Four subprojects each run a runReload fork. Every fork prints the same line
# (SHARED_BANNER) plus a per-project unique marker. Running reloadOutput scoped
# to ONE subproject (a) should show only that subproject's fork, but it reports
# every running fork in the config, so the shared line shows up once per
# subproject (4x) and the other projects' output leaks in.

# Start runReload forks in all four subprojects.
> a/runReload
> b/runReload
> c/runReload
> d/runReload
> a/waitForStart
> b/waitForStart
> c/waitForStart
> d/waitForStart

# Ask for subproject a's output only.
> a/reloadOutput

# Assert a/reloadOutput reported ONLY project a (SHARED_BANNER once, no b/c/d markers).
# Fails today: SHARED_BANNER appears 4x and UNIQUE_B/C/D leak in.
> a/assertOnlyOwnOutput
